            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0606" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European. War 1939/5999: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-12T12:00:00+01:00">October 12,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 12—9:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Source of information believed to be reliable and close to Government at
                    Rabat from member of which he [<hi rendition="#italic">it?</hi>] is reported
                    that Axis requested Spanish Minister of the Interior not to make trouble in
                    Morocco at the present juncture as Italo-Germans desired to concentrate on
                    Eastern Mediterranean.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
